<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Unicafe sees 19.7-22.5 mln bag coffee crop.</title>
<headline>Brazil Unicafe sees 19.7-22.5 mln bag coffee crop.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1997/98 coffee crop is expected to between 19.7 million and 22.5 million 60-kg bags, according to the first estimate from Unicafe, Brazil's leading exporter.</p>
<p>Of this, between 13.6 million and 15.6 million bags will be Group I coffees, 2.2 million to 2.5 million bags Group II coffee and 3.9 million and 4.4 million bags conillon, Unicafe said.</p>
<p>A breakdown of Unicafe's estimate by state follows.</p>
<p>	 STATE	   LOWEST EST     HIGHEST EST</p>
<p>    Espirito Santo	3.40	     3.80</p>
<p>    (Arabica		0.80	     1.00)</p>
<p>    (Conillon	     2.60	     2.80)</p>
<p>    Sao Paulo	     2.70	     3.00</p>
<p>    Minas Gerais	  8.80	     9.90</p>
<p>    (South		  5.00	     5.30)</p>
<p>    (Cerrado		2.00	     2.30)</p>
<p>    (Zona Da Mata	 1.50	     1.80)</p>
<p>    (Others		 0.30	     0.50)</p>
